      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Treat higher concurrency as a workload-dependent tuning option. The reference says insertion workers may improve speed, while MongoDB support guidance recommends changing concurrency when resources are not already maxed out and notes that restore must recreate data files and indexes. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongorestore.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:1f76df183d9568772b81066919595e8b130d4dc661a229a867f8c0406405f706",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
