          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/community/forums/t/why-mongodump-or-mongorestore-so-slow/179754"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Compression trades CPU work for less output I/O: MongoDB support guidance says --gzip can reduce disk-write I/O when CPU is available, while the historical TOOLS-997 reporter says gzip CPU usage made backups take longer. Neither establishes a universal restore-speed gain from gzip. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/community/forums/t/why-mongodump-or-mongorestore-so-slow/179754",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:1f6d479b6d53b5b9cf340b418e7becedc7cccb7d8461e4b74f6f0b1cd5037787",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
