            "ev:82db19ed610d25ebe4cf9da130a83659678073299b28a567e999d9ac2659b524"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/TOOLS-997"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the MongoDB community performance discussion, Stennie says --gzip can reduce dump-write I/O when CPU is available, while restore must recreate data files and rebuild indexes. The advice is to adjust restore concurrency when resources are not already maxed out; these are conditional tuning choices. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/community/forums/t/why-mongodump-or-mongorestore-so-slow/179754",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ba4f9303ea2e817c44ea12c54708b81ee962c493bf16c1d04b418fe851e98819",
